#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133729 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbc399b-90f3-5acd-ac70-7345a8436978" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using a CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e338a7c-f5c5-55b6-800b-47f10296b1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112}{729}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499686} {:answer/id #uuid "4673f4bc-028d-52bd-b6cb-43a313197f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{1458}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499785} {:answer/id #uuid "60d5eb82-e934-5a50-abfb-6bb988e212e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{230}{729}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499844} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8b3642-18a5-59b9-ba90-c44b1dc2ff93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{130}{729}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499989} {:answer/id #uuid "b05849a6-fd14-5761-ac6a-f3df6f46c897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{113}{1458}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60d5eb82-e934-5a50-abfb-6bb988e212e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{230}{729}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499844} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc71117-bad7-5cf6-bbde-8b45ac8873de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2175ed2b-85f5-5f4e-9b21-fd44965b957e" :question/math-academy-id "q-126173" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1458}, & 0\\le x\\le 9 \\\\ 1, & x>9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(1<X\\le 3).$" :question/worked-solution "We can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 3) & =P(X\\le 3)-P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =F(3)-F(1) \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{6}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{1458})-(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{1458}) \\\\  & =\\frac{230}{729}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-x^{2}+8x-7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da4529e7-604e-506b-adaa-ff85312c20f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-x^{2}+8x-7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442316} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ff772f-b783-5f66-89ac-69df3d1d8f2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-210785" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{8}{9},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}(-\\frac{2}{9}t+\\frac{8}{9})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(-\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}x-\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}({x}^{2}-8x+7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7), & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "095360e1-dd96-5383-931f-a201eff47a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419857} {:answer/id #uuid "170a0edf-da7f-5652-903d-c47b4ac8c342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1+\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419864} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8d1627-2737-5252-95ce-1a7d32a52868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{1+{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419871} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0ae796-f204-5f28-ae72-68cb7f93938e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1+\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419873} {:answer/id #uuid "cfec970b-e672-5e0e-a27f-c56e83e7f7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfec970b-e672-5e0e-a27f-c56e83e7f7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x)=1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419918} :answer-field/id #uuid "f84d8dbb-e4a3-55af-a310-662430392d90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae38bc39-2bd5-58c3-af2b-ad65de482c6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89635" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{(1+{e}^{x})^{3}},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{(1+{e}^{t})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{t})^{2}}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{(1+{e}^{x})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eedcfa3d-b02b-5f96-99f4-cd0a452d272a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a CDF Given a PDF With Lower and Upper Bounds"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2dedee-a9a6-5f08-aaca-929e3c0e1a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-8x-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499679} {:answer/id #uuid "215bd0d9-f220-5e68-82fa-30f7f2f20f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+8x-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499729} {:answer/id #uuid "6f65d4dc-2c09-5761-b57d-65243b8be70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-8x-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499863} {:answer/id #uuid "9697c8ec-2113-54d6-875d-643ae67cf997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-{x}^{2}+8x-15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499949} {:answer/id #uuid "ea81b801-f204-59da-86c8-5fb92620fdc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-8x-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "215bd0d9-f220-5e68-82fa-30f7f2f20f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+8x-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499729} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4dd9342-bbc6-5cbd-86b8-630a593c1561" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "471d1d77-25cd-5101-acd9-2310f0d5d168" :question/math-academy-id "q-89672" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2(-x+4),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<3 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $3\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{x}2(-t+4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={8t-{t}^{2}|}_{3}^{x} \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}+8x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ -{x}^{2}+8x-15, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b0ce833-e045-5aff-94a4-f9ad56cdb904" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a CDF Given a PDF That’s Nonzero Over All Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "492f777b-8264-55ab-9be1-d1359bd9513d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424871} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7a5540-6762-5260-9b7f-2a98061bf95e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424872} {:answer/id #uuid "50e4b7f0-64ef-587b-bfde-a4520b836560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424873} {:answer/id #uuid "d60102cb-368c-5209-b3c3-06d9c44b89a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424880} {:answer/id #uuid "ef55c585-a616-50c9-9382-ffb7b5a8ceda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef55c585-a616-50c9-9382-ffb7b5a8ceda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424881} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce55fccd-c2b9-544b-881d-b59a7e7c0f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b70eaac-0c45-5da5-8a2f-2002d9071035" :question/math-academy-id "q-89727" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{-|x/3|}}{6},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
